enchilada: GPU: clean and invalidate only what the CPU wrote or will read (~50 MB of dc civac a frame)

Boot 5x (2026-11-05 21:24, CoreAnimation animating at 21 swaps/s, measured over SSH): backboardd's
render thread had 18.9 s of kernel time for ~4200 frames (~4.5 ms a frame), and eagl.c's "waiting"
(glFinish) was 5.3 ms of a 6.9 ms frame of 8 draws and 16 triangles (12.5 ms for the 7-19 draw frames
of a touch). Per frame SUBMIT cleaned every BO and in-place surface it named (the 11 MB display surface
and Mesa's 12 MB render target, every texture surface), WAIT_FENCE cleaned+invalidated them again,
and zcFlip settled and cleaned the display surface once more: ~50 MB of cache maintenance a frame.

- SUBMIT cleans an arena BO only if the client mapped it (clientMemoryForType: its stores may be in
  the cache) or it was never cleaned (the allocator zeroes through a cacheable alias). An in-place
  surface is cleaned when this import never cleaned it, the client mapped it, its seed moved (a
  writer unlocked it), or sweetgpuage ms (default 50) have passed: writers that never lock, the
  fallback HakiOS's hakios.gpu.cpp keeps too. A scanout-pool surface (CoreAnimation's GL display
  surface: once imported only the GPU draws it) is cleaned once.
- WAIT_FENCE invalidates only BOs the client mapped; every other CPU reader settles for itself
  (IOSurface lock, panel copy, CPU_PREP, BO_SYNC), and a BO's first mapping invalidates it.
- zcFlip of a GPU-imported surface waits for its fence and touches no cache lines
  (sweet_surface_gpu_wait): the MDP reads memory and the CPU never wrote the surface.
- IOSurface lock with kIOSurfaceLockAvoidSync (0x2) skips the settle (the scanout write wait stays):
  eagl.c (ios-op6-gpu gles-ca/eagl-lock-avoidsync.patch) locks each frame's display surface only to
  move its seed.
- Fence waits past 2 ms poll every 250 us instead of every 1 ms (the GPU raises no interrupt here).
- One line every 10 s while submitting: "SWEET GPU: last N ms: S submits; cache maintenance X MB in
  Y us, Z MB left alone (0310); W fence waits, avg A us, max M us".

Boot-arg sweetgpuflush=1: everything at every SUBMIT, wait, flip and lock as before (also the
first thing to try if pictures show stale content); sweetgpuage=0: textures cleaned at every SUBMIT.

